<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hadibu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tamrida</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hadibu, formerly Tamrida, is the main town of the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socotra">Socotra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, on its north coast. It was a seat of the Mahra sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qishn">Qishn</a> and Socotra, who ruled the island from the 15th century until 1967. Today it is the administrative centre of the Socotra archipelago.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hadibu.jpg" alt="Hadibu" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rod Waddington from Kergunyah, Australia · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mosque,_Hadibo,_Socotra_Island_(11007460353).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
